	"title"		"More Zone Blocks v1.0"
	"description"		"[h1]🏗️ MORE ZONE BLOCKS v1.0 🏗️[/h1]
[b]The Definitive 64K Zone Block Limit Breaker for Cities: Skylines[/b]
[i]Engineered with Two-Stream Vanilla Save Preservation, 64-Block Simulation Pacing, and Universal Stream Armor by NgocDuy[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]🌟 WHAT IS THIS MOD?[/h1]
Have you ever hit the invisible [b]Zone Block limit[/b] while building a sprawling metropolis or expanding your regional highway and transit network?
In vanilla Cities: Skylines, [b]ZoneManager.MAX_BLOCK_COUNT is hardcoded at 49,152 blocks (48K)[/b].
When you build extensive road networks—especially when using [b]More Nodes/Segments (64K)[/b] or [b]81 Tiles 2[/b]—every road segment generates up to 4 Zone Blocks. Once you cross ~22,000 segments, the 49,152 Zone Block ceiling is completely exhausted!

[b]The Consequence:[/b]
New roads lose their zoning grids completely (no colored zoning squares appear), road placement tools freeze, and buildings cannot grow.

[b]More Zone Blocks v1.0[/b] breaks this barrier, safely expanding the internal Zone Block capacity to [b]65,535 blocks (64K)[/b] — giving you [b]+16,383 additional Zone Blocks (+33.3% capacity)[/b]!

[list]
[*] [b]Vanilla Limit:[/b] 49,152 Zone Blocks
[*] [b]More Zone Blocks Limit:[/b] [b]65,535 Zone Blocks (16-bit Maximum Ceiling)[/b]
[*] [b]Savegame Safety:[/b] [b]Two-Stream Vanilla Preservation (100% Safe to load without mods)[/b]
[*] [b]Simulation Guarantee:[/b] 64-Block frame pacing ensures buildings grow properly on all extended blocks
[*] [b]Stream Armor:[/b] Exact IL stream bounds protection preventing downstream manager desynchronization
[*] [b]Deadlock Shield:[/b] Integrated loading profiler safeguards against DayNightProperties and essential scene freezes
[*] [b]Backward Compatibility:[/b] Seamlessly loads vanilla saves, 64K saves, and 128K extended saves
[*] [b]Compatibility:[/b] 100% compatible with 81 Tiles 2, More Nodes/Segments, Zoning Adjuster, Move It, Network Anarchy, and RICO
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]⚡ KEY ARCHITECTURAL ADVANTAGES[/h1]

[list]
[*] [b]Safe 16-Bit Architecture (Zero Overflow):[/b]
    By expanding to 65,535 (0xFFFF), all internal pointers in [i]NetSegment[/i], [i]ZoneBlock[/i], and [i]ZoneManager[/i] remain native [b]ushort[/b]. No memory layout corruption, no struct bloat, and zero CPU register overflow.

[*] [b]Two-Stream Save Preservation (Zero Dangling Pointers):[/b]
    Before saving, block pointers >= 49,152 in [i]NetSegment[/i] are temporarily sanitized to 0 for the vanilla save stream, while their mapping and full data are safely packaged into a custom Sidecar Stream ([i]MoreZoneBlocks_Extended[/i]).
    [b]Result:[/b] Your savegame can be opened on vanilla or unmodded installations without triggering fatal [i]IndexOutOfRangeException[/i] crashes! When loaded with More Zone Blocks, all 65K blocks and segment linkages are seamlessly restored.

[*] [b]IL Stream Alignment & Deserialization Defense-in-Depth:[/b]
    During deserialization, a surgical IL transpiler on [i]ZoneManager.Data.Deserialize[/i] clamps the buffer read bound to exactly 49,152 blocks. This prevents a critical 461 KB stream overread, guaranteeing 100% clean stream alignment for PropManager, TreeManager, WeatherManager, and all subsequent managers.

[*] [b]Loading Screen Deadlock Shield:[/b]
    Armed with bounded-timeout protection against [i]DayNightProperties[/i] coroutine hangs and [i]WaitUntilEssentialScenesLoaded[/i] lockups, ensuring game loading never freezes even with large mod lists and hundreds of custom assets.

[*] [b]64-Block Frame Pacing (100% Simulation Coverage):[/b]
    Vanilla's [i]ZoneManager.SimulationStepImpl[/i] only steps 48 blocks per frame (1,024 x 48 = 49,152). We re-engineered the pacing to [b]64 blocks per frame (1,024 x 64 = 65,536)[/b].
    [b]Result:[/b] All extended blocks receive active simulation ticks, allowing residential, commercial, industrial, and office zones to grow naturally.

[*] [b]18 Inlined Loop Guards Neutralized:[/b]
    Patched hardcoded 49,152 loop break thresholds across [i]ZoneBlock[/i], [i]Building.CheckZoning[/i], [i]ZoneTool[/i], [i]DefaultTool[/i], and [i]BuildingTool[/i], permanently eliminating [i]Invalid list detected![/i] error spam.

[*] [b]Simulation-Thread Safe Auto-GC:[/b]
    Background garbage collector runs exclusively on the simulation thread (16 segments/tick), safely purging orphaned, unzoned blocks on highways, freeways, elevated viaducts, and rail corridors to keep your block pool clean and lag-free.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]🧩 COMPATIBILITY[/h1]
Tested and fully compatible with the modern modding ecosystem:
[list]
[*] [b]Harmony 2.2+[/b] (Required dependency)
[*] [b]More Nodes/Segments (v5.1.4+)[/b] (Perfect synergy)
[*] [b]81 Tiles 2[/b] (Coexistence architecture: respects 270 x 270 zone grid)
[*] [b]Zoning Adjuster[/b]
[*] [b]Network Anarchy[/b]
[*] [b]Move It[/b]
[*] [b]Find It! 2[/b]
[*] [b]Plop the Growables & Ploppable RICO Revisited[/b]
[*] [b]TM:PE (Traffic Manager)[/b]
[*] [b]Adaptive Roads & Network Skins[/b]
[*] [b]More Props BETA / More Props[/b]
[*] [b]More Vehicles Renew[/b]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]📋 REQUIREMENTS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2040656402]Harmony 2.2.2-0 (CitiesHarmony)[/url]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[i]Developed with precision and care for the Cities: Skylines community by NgocDuy.[/i]"
	"changenote"		"[v1.0.1 Hotfix & Stability Update]
- Fixed save stream desynchronization during deserialization: Added IL transpiler on ZoneManager.Data.Deserialize to clamp reading buffer bound to exactly 49,152 blocks, permanently resolving downstream stream misalignment (WeatherManager tag mismatches, Prop/Tree corruption).
- Added Universal StreamTagShield for 2-string LoadingProfiler overloads.
- Added DayNightDeadlockShield with bounded-timeout protection against DayNightProperties loading screen freezes.
- Added exception armor for BuildingManager.RefreshStyleBuildings to prevent simulation failure from missing workshop assets.
- Backward Compatibility: Full support for loading saves created with 128K extended formats, safely remapping to 64K.
- Tested and verified 100% working on large mega-cities!"
}
